    "interpretation": "The pinned R580 source gives a conditional route for a foreign tracker into the PMM wait. After migration, UVM selects policy/accessed-by processors and loops over their mappings into one local output tracker. Each GPU mapping acquires against the shared VA-block tracker but appends its push to that local tracker; the migration caller later merges the local tracker into the VA-block tracker. VA-block chunk cleanup can pass that shared tracker into the PMM root tracker, and the next ordinary no-eviction allocation calls the foreign-GPU CPU wait while the VA-block lock is held. This is conditionally reachable when multiple GPU IDs are registered and accessible in one VA space, even though direct cross-GPU push dependencies are rejected. The current hybrid frontend still blocks second-provider UVM registration, so this exact V100+Blackwell route has not run on hardware. The source path is not proof of a deadlock: completion dependence on UVM progress is unmeasured. A simple early error is unsafe to assume because the PMM error path deinitializes the collected tracker and frees chunks, and pending GPU use has not been ruled out.",
